Third-party material under vendor/
=================================

The two directories below are crates.io packages of salsa, copied as published and then patched for
the fork Engine (D11). They are not workspace members (`exclude = ["vendor"]` in the workspace
manifest); the workspace uses them through `[patch.crates-io]`, so every crate of the process that
depends on `salsa` or `salsa-macro-rules`, rust-analyzer's included, builds against these copies.

Origin
------

    crate salsa             0.28.5 sha256:27d2e6e19e39591cd99c01ac4141544b4d012cfd0831348629b8187fa9fe6d34
    crate salsa-macro-rules 0.28.5 sha256:baf90a551c38f25ed8489111d3d5827aa18e1b85963f5e6a298505b1d1e2cb7e

- Source: the crates.io packages `salsa-0.28.5.crate` and `salsa-macro-rules-0.28.5.crate`. The
  sha256 is the package checksum the workspace Cargo.lock recorded for each before the patch.
  `just salsa-upstream` reads the `crate` lines above.
- Upstream repository: https://github.com/salsa-rs/salsa
- Not vendored: `salsa-macros` 0.28.5, which stays a crates.io dependency.
- Left out of the copy: `.cargo-ok` and `.cargo_vcs_info.json`, which cargo writes into an
  unpacked package and which are not source.

Terms
-----

Both packages are distributed under `MIT OR Apache-2.0` (their manifests say
`Apache-2.0 OR MIT`), the same terms as this repository. Each directory keeps the package's
`LICENSE-APACHE` and `LICENSE-MIT` unchanged; `vendor/salsa` keeps its `README.md`
(`salsa-macro-rules` ships none). Those files must stay.

Changes
-------

Every change to a vendored file is marked. A changed hunk contains the mark `// ryo-v2 fork:`
(Rust) or `# ryo-v2 fork:` (TOML) on an added line, saying why; new code goes in its own module,
`vendor/salsa/src/fork/`, whose files start with the mark. `just salsa-upstream` diffs each
directory against its crates.io package, hunk by hunk with no context lines, and fails on any hunk
without the mark, on a removed-only hunk, and on a binary difference.

One file is exempt from the diff: `Cargo.lock`. `vendor/salsa/Cargo.lock` is regenerated by cargo
for the path dependency on `../salsa-macro-rules` (a lock file keeps no comments); the suite runs
with `--locked`, so it cannot drift from the manifest.

Upstream's own test suite (`vendor/salsa/tests/`) runs on the patched copy, on the toolchain salsa
ships for it (`vendor/salsa/rust-toolchain.toml`, kept as shipped), with `just salsa-upstream`;
`just pre-push` runs it.
